  "problem": {
    "id": "train-3940",
    "question": "Every 4 weeks, Helen hand washes her silk pillowcases.  It takes 30 minutes to hand wash all of them.  In 1 year, how much time does Helen spend hand washing her pillowcases?",
    "gold": "390",
    "answer": "She hand washes them every 4 weeks and there are 52 weeks in a year so she washes them 52/4 = <<52/4=13>>13 times per year\nIt takes her 30 minutes to hand wash the pillowcases and she does this 13 times per year for a total of 30*13 = <<30*13=390>>390 minutes per year\n#### 390"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much time Helen spends hand washing her pillowcases in one year, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of 4-week periods in one year.\n2. Determine the total time spent hand washing the pillowcases in one year.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the number of 4-week periods in one year.**\n\nThere are 52 weeks in a year. Since Helen hand washes her pillowcases every 4 weeks, we divide 52 by 4:\n\\[\n\\frac{52}{4} = 13\n\\]\nSo, there are 13 periods of 4 weeks in one year.\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total time spent hand washing the pillowcases in one year.**\n\nIt takes Helen 30 minutes to hand wash all of her pillowcases. Since she does this 13 times in one year, we multiply 30 minutes by 13:\n\\[\n30 \\times 13 = 390\n\\]\nSo, Helen spends 390 minutes hand washing her pillowcases in one year.\n\nTo convert 390 minutes into hours, we divide by 60 (since there are 60 minutes in an hour):\n\\[\n\\frac{390}{60} = 6.5\n\\]\nSo, Helen spends 6.5 hours hand washing her pillowcases in one year.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6.5}\n\\]",
